cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  When the Treatment Talks Back: Information Limits of Observational Logs from
  Adaptive Generative Political Communication
message: If you use this material, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Park
    given-names: Kun Woo
    affiliation: Kookmin University
repository-code: https://github.com/kunhailP/when-treatment-talks-back
abstract: >-
  Replication material for a paper on what conversation logs from an adaptive
  generative system can identify about the system's turn-level behavior. The
  efficiency bound for the turn-level excursion effect grows exponentially in a
  policy decisiveness index identified from logs; along policy sequences whose
  decisiveness grows with sample size the minimax risk is bounded away from
  zero; and the overlap mass that survives localizes on the policy's learned
  decision boundary, leaving a regression-discontinuity estimand.
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - semiparametric efficiency
  - minimax lower bounds
  - overlap
  - micro-randomized trials
  - political persuasion
  - large language models
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-08-31'
version: v0.3
